---
description: Gradion Book Illustration Studio — project constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

This is a take-home fullstack app. Keep it small.

- Pipeline is the Colab notebook section "Illustrate a book: The Wind in the Willows" steps 1–5 only.
- Hard caps, enforced on the server: 2 adult characters, 1 chapter.
- User-driven steps in order. No auto-retry of Gemini. Send the book once (file + interaction chain).
- JSON files on disk. Per-project in-process mutex around read–modify–write, not around the API call.
- `status` is pipeline progress. `stepState` is IDLE | RUNNING. Failed steps stay on the same status with `lastError`.
- Illustration consistency is image-chat chaining (path A), not attaching portrait bytes.
- UI must cover app-demo.html (Gradion tokens, screens, running/error/stuck). Polling while RUNNING.
- Do not implement Veo, Lyria, TTS, SSE, or public deploy.
